window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-063", "name_zh": "暗示", "name_en": "Suggestion", "tagline": "你一天到晚在心里自说自话的那些话，就是你收到的最重要的暗示——它跟构成物质实相的是同一种材料，所以它能改架构；别人的话有没有用，最后取决于你信不信。", "explanation": "暗示是赛斯实相制造机制的关键词，但它的意思和催眠舞台秀那种「被控制」刚好相反。定义很朴素：暗示是针对某个行为或假设的一句话，本身没有魔法——重复得够多、又被热切相信，就会变成不再被检验的深刻习性。要紧的是两句升级语：第一，形成暗示的材料与形成物质实相的材料相同，所以暗示真能改变架构，心理暗示是一切实相形成的基础；第二，你收到的最重要暗示不是别人给的，是你自己有意识的信念，是心里那台从早到晚的自说自话。因此医生的负面预言能经由你的恐惧长成真正的病，维生素的效力也只维持到你不再相信为止；而睡前暗示、对第二天活动的预期画面、同情地对自己被吓怕的部分说话，都是可以直接上手的配方。珍和罗拿它做日常实验：出体、记得梦、疗愈梦、改善与父母的反应，成败都有记录。赛斯还用了这个词的另一面——凡是被说出的，都暗示着没说出的：语言骑在无声上，肉体生命暗示非肉体的源头，群体事件暗示一张内在沟通网。读赛斯，一半是读他说的，一半是读他暗示的。", "definitions": [{"zh": "暗示往往是直接对一个特殊行为或假设的声明。并没有魔法与暗示相连——但这种暗示，当重复得够多，且被热切地相信时，的确会呈现出一种深切的习惯性。它们不再被检验，却被认为是刻板的真实。", "en": "Suggestions are usually statements directed toward a particular action or hypothesis. There is no magic connected with suggestions — but repeated often enough, and believed in fervently, such suggestions do indeed take on a deeply habitual nature. They are no longer examined, but taken for literal truth.", "source": "Session 5"}, {"zh": "你自己有意识的信念，就是你接到的最重要「暗示」。也就是说，你接受或拒绝所有其他的意念，是看你是否相信它们是真的，而那是根据一天大部分时间在你心中不断进行地自说自话——你自己给自己的暗示——来决定的。", "en": "Your own conscious beliefs are the most important suggestions that you receive. All other ideas are rejected or accepted according to whether or not you believe they are true, in line with the steady conscious chattering that goes on within your mind most of the day — the suggestions given to you by yourself.", "source": "Session 615"}, {"zh": "因为形成暗示的材料跟形成你们物质实相的材料是一样的，所以暗示的确可以改变你们在其中运作的那个架构。", "en": "Because suggestions are formed of the same stuff that forms your physical reality, suggestions can indeed change the framework within which you operate.", "source": "Session 187"}, {"zh": "你们通过暗示与预期来形成你们的物质实相。你们在潜意识与意识的层面上，经验你们预期要经验的东西。", "en": "You form your physical reality through suggestion and expectation. You experience what you expect to experience at a subconscious and a conscious level.", "source": "Session 493"}, {"zh": "心理暗示事实上就是所有实相形成的基础。", "en": "Mental suggestion is indeed the basis upon which all reality is founded.", "source": "Session 170"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "暗示到底是什么：一句重复到不用再检查的话", "note": "AI总结：暗示通常就是直接针对某个行为或假设的一句话，跟着理智走——「如果事情是如此这般，那么必然如此」。它本身没有魔法，但重复得够多、又被热切地相信时，就会变成一种深切的习性：你不再检验它，直接把它当刻板的真理。赛斯更进一步说：心理暗示事实上是所有实相形成的基础，因为形成暗示的材料和形成你物质实相的材料是同一种东西，所以暗示真的能改变你运作于其中的那个架构。流行说法爱讲你随时随处都被暗示摆布，赛斯的版本刚好相反：你自己有意识的信念，才是你收到的最重要的暗示——其他意念接不接受，全看你信不信它是真的，而那取决于你一天大部分时间在心里不断进行的自说自话。所以担心暗示会造成某个结果反而愚蠢：正是暗示造成了你所看见的一切，你在潜意识和意识两个层面经验你预期要经验的东西。判断：暗示不是外来的咒语，它是你制造实相的日常工序。", "src": "第 5、160、170、187、422、493、615、622 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 5 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 160 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 170 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 187 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 422 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 493 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 615 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 622 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0196", "zh": "在这些能力的发展中，暗示当然扮演一定的角色。即使我们的课已进展到这个程度，但还是不容易让你们完全了解暗示的基本性质为何，不过等到你们更深入这个主题后，就会有一些实验可以让你们俩来试试。", "en": "Suggestion would of course play a part in the development of these abilities. It is difficult, even though we are so far into our sessions, to give you any full understanding yet of what is involved in the basic nature of suggestion, but as we go deeper into the subject there will be experiments that you both can try.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第160节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "160", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0237", "zh": "就像我告诉过你的，我是个教育家，因此我最关心的是教育，是想法。所有你想知道的我都会确切告诉你，假如你要听个过瘾，就得接受我的一些用语，因为我也很愿意接受你的用语，这大部分与你对暗示理论的想法有关。如果你读一读我们的一些资料，就会清楚知道，心理暗示事实上就是所有实相形成的基础。", "en": "I am as I told you an educator, and as such my main concern is with education, is with ideas. I want to tell you exactly what you want to know, and if you will hear me then to a large measure you will have to accept some of my terms, for I am quite willing to accept some of yours. Much of this has to do with your idea of the theory of suggestion. If you would read some of our material, it would then become obvious to you that mental suggestion is indeed the basis upon which all reality is founded.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第170节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "170", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0298", "zh": "因为形成暗示的材料跟形成你们物质实相的材料是一样的，所以暗示的确可以改变你们在其中运作的那个架构。这不是胡言乱语，我提供了很多方法和手段，如果能遵循我的建议，就可以强力证实我们资料的可行性。", "en": "Because suggestions are formed of the same stuff that forms your physical reality, suggestions can indeed change the framework within which you operate. This is no Pollyanna hogwash. Many of the ways and the means have been given. My suggestions, if followed, will be fair enough proof of the validity of our material.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第187节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "187", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0601", "zh": "你看，在这个时候写这首诗这个行为，不论诗的讯息是什么，都代表着一种意愿，愿意让自发的自己表达出来。而诗的讯息本身又加倍强化了这个暗示。就连第一段里的那种情绪——自发地表达出来、又创造性地形成为艺术——也是一个好迹象。", "en": "The act of writing the poem at this time, regardless of the poem's message, you see, represents a willingness to allow the spontaneous self expression. The message itself then doubly reinforces the suggestion. Even the emotion in the first portion, spontaneously expressed and creatively formed into art, is a good indication.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第422节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "422", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0671", "zh": "现在。你们只看见自己愿意看见的，而把暗示当作你们所见之物的结果或起因，那是愚蠢。在课堂上担心暗示会招致某个特定结果，也是愚蠢……因为正是暗示造成了你们所看见的一切。你们通过暗示与预期来形成你们的物质实相。你们在潜意识与意识的层面上，经验你们预期要经验的东西。因此，正如鲁柏极小心地不让暗示掺夹其中，他也让你们变得过分谨慎了；正因这个缘故，课堂上你们错失了许多机会……这些就是我今晚早些时候谈过的那些赌注。你们本有能力看见比你们实际所见的更多的东西，而你们是有这个能力的。你享受自己的被动状态（对[CW]说），到了欢喜交付、全然放手的地步；而其实，你们看，被动之中有一个点，在那里你是被动而警觉的。你却越过了那个点，于是失去了你本可以看见的东西。就像我们这位在场的朋友越过了那个点（指[TM]），看着那些肖像，然后有意识地……因为你并没有先做出原初的直觉判断……而是有意识地按国籍、年龄，以及你想到的种种条件，去端详那些肖像。", "en": "Now, you see what you are willing to see, and it is stupidity to consider suggestion as the result or the cause of what you see. It is stupidity in class to worry that suggestion would cause a given result... for suggestion causes whatever you see. You form your physical reality through suggestion and expectation. You experience what you expect to experience at a subconscious and a conscious level. And therefore as Ruburt is very careful that suggestion is not involved, so he has also had you be overly cautious, and there have been many opportunities in class that you have missed for this reason... and these are the bets that I have spoken about earlier this evening. You have the ability to see more than you saw, and you have the ability. You enjoyed your passivity (to CW) to the point of a joyous giving-up; and instead, you see, there is a point within passivity where you are passively alert. And you went beyond the point and lost what you might have seen. As our friend here went beyond the point (referring to TM), looked at the portraits and consciously... for you did not make an original intuitive judgment... but consciously looked at those portraits in terms of nationality, age, and all the requirements that you thought of.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第493节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "493", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0760", "zh": "有很多文章都说到“暗示”（suggestion）的本质和重要性。近期来流行的说法之一是，你随时随地都受到暗示的支配。其实，你自己有意识的信念，就是你接到的最重要“暗示”。也就是说，你接受或拒绝所有其他的意念，是看你是否相信它们是真的，而那是根据一天大部分时间在你心中不断进行地自说自话——你自己给自己的暗示——来决定的。", "en": "(10:06. Seth-Jane, deep in thought, paused.) Much has been written about the nature and importance of suggestion. One of the current ideas in vogue holds that you are constantly at the mercy of suggestion. Your own conscious beliefs are the most important suggestions that you receive. All other ideas are rejected or accepted according to whether or not you believe they are true, in line with the steady conscious chattering that goes on within your mind most of the day — the suggestions given to you by yourself.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第615节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "615", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0770", "zh": "先前我用过“我是个负责的父亲（母亲）”作为信念的一个例子。（见第三章第六一八节。）如果对你而言，这是指：“我花了极大心力一定要我的孩子记得刷牙、吃得够饱，并且举止适度。”那么你就将以那种看法来诠释“越来越好”的暗示。", "en": "Earlier I used, “I am a dependable parent,” as an example of a belief. (See the 618th session in Chapter Three.) If to you this means, “I give great attention to seeing that my children brush their teeth, eat enough, and perform properly,” then you will interpret the “better and better” suggestion in that light.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第622节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "622", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1091", "zh": "暗示（suggestion）往往是直接对一个特殊行为或假设的声明。到一个很大的程度，暗示是跟随理智的命令，而与有意识的思考过程结合为一体的。举例来说：“如果事情是如此这般，那么必然会如此。”并没有魔法与暗示相连——但这种暗示，当重复得够多，且被热切地相信时，的确会呈现出一种深切的习惯性。它们不再被检验，却被认为是刻板的真实。", "en": "Suggestions are usually statements directed toward a particular action or hypothesis. To a large extent, suggestions are tied into conscious thought processes, following the dictates of reason. For example: “If thus and thus be so, then thus and thus must follow.” There is no magic connected with suggestions — but repeated often enough, and believed in fervently, such suggestions do indeed take on a deeply habitual nature. They are no longer examined, but taken for literal truth.", "source": "健康之道 · 第5节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "5", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1101", "zh": "不过，人们不会不管愿不愿意地被一个或另一个负面暗示所动摇。每个人都有一整团的信念和暗示——而这些都相当一个萝卜一个坑地反映在肉体本身上。", "en": "People are not simply swung willy-nilly by one negative suggestion or another, however. Each person has an entire body of beliefs and suggestions — and these are quite literally reflected in the physical body itself.", "source": "健康之道 · 第5节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "5", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "负面暗示的破坏力：医生一句话，身体当真", "note": "AI总结：情绪里有恐惧时，那种不经思考、只凭最稀薄证据就做出的暗示破坏力最强：心跳稍微不规则这种无害状况，可以被医师一句无心的话，透过病人的恐惧变成真正的功能失调；牙医若说「你这样下去牙齿保不住」，当事人多半会照办——身体照着糟糕的预期去实现。在医院环境里这种事成批出现：医生预告很长一段复原期，负面暗示主宰现在、又被投射到将来，仿佛每个人都迟早会病；连预防性检查也带着同一套逻辑——你被告知自己处在随时会出差错的身体机能的掌握之下。原罪这类宗教负面暗示是同一个机制的文化版。对抗之道不是硬扛：许多人拼命「否定」别人的负面建议、改喊正面口号，其实恰恰因为他们深信负面信念的力量更强。还有一个反直觉的提醒：梦一直在给你健康问题的线索，连理由和解法都给——只是你没有能利用它的文化习惯。判断：负面暗示的效力不在说者，在你交出去的相信。", "src": "第 1、18、98、374、487、646、660、763、805、922 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 1 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 18 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 98 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 374 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 487 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 646 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 660 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 763 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 805 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 922 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0013", "zh": "这就是自我不屈不挠的一种有意识姿态，不要与柔软灵活的潜意识抽离混为一谈，后者实际上温暖、有弹性又广阔。也就是说，在它的内在可以容纳很多元素，承认它们，但不要受不好的或是负面的暗示或元素影响。", "en": "This is an unbending conscious pose of the ego, and not to be confused with the lithe subconscious detachment which is actually warm, flexible and expansive. That is, it can contain within it many elements, acknowledge them but be not affected by bad or negative suggestions or elements.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第18节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "18", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0139", "zh": "我会进一步说，其实鲁柏在整脊师那里的确有机会发脾气，因为在情绪有恐惧的时候，像他那种不经思考，只凭最稀薄的证据就做出的暗示，可能导致的伤害和破坏力最强。而在一个不设防、情绪沮丧，尤其是面临压力的人格身上，这样的暗示可能导致一颗具有保护作用的无害结节，被不利的、或不如说被很糟的预期这股强大力量改变，转变成人格害怕的形式；就像心跳稍微不规则这种无害的状况，因为一个医师不经思考的暗示，就可能透过病人的恐惧而变成一个真正的功能失调，同样的，暗示也可能把鲁柏这类相对无害的构造转变成关节炎的状况。", "en": "I would state furthermore that indeed Ruburt did have occasion to be angry at the chiropractor, since with an emotional fear unthinking suggestions such as his, made with only the flimsiest of evidence, can be most harmful and destructive. And in an unwary, emotionally upset personality, particularly if under stress, such a suggestion could cause a harmless and protective nodule to be changed by the strong powers of adverse expectation, or rather expectation poorly used, into the form of what is feared; as a slight but harmless irregularity of heartbeat, with the unthinking suggestion of a doctor, can become through the patient’s fears an actual functional disorder, so could suggestion turn a relatively harmless formation like Ruburt’s into an arthritic condition.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第98节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "98", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0554", "zh": "灵性环境仍然有待改善，丈夫已经很努力，不过，必须尽最大的努力。早上和晚上应该再特别注意，以免产生负面暗示的氛围。（停顿）继续使用花生油和遵循其他建议，现在一定要把苜蓿加进来。", "en": "The psychic environment still needs to be improved. The husband has made good efforts. However, stronger ones must be made. Particular care should be taken in the morning and evening, so that there is no atmosphere of negative suggestion. (Pause.) Continue the peanut oil and the other recommendations. The alfalfa should definitely be added now.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第374节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "374", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0657", "zh": "倘若这位牙医两年前就看过鲁柏[Ruburt]的口腔，他会大为震惊，并且告诉鲁柏，到如今他脑袋上不会剩下一颗牙了。而鲁柏极可能对那样的暗示起反应。", "en": "Had the man seen Ruburt’s mouth two years ago he would have been outraged, and told Ruburt he would not have a tooth left in his head by now. And Ruburt most likely would have reacted to the suggestion.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第487节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "487", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0791", "zh": "你可能觉得，你的宗教信仰与你的健康或日常经验没什么关系，你们那些离开了有组织宗教的人，也许觉得很不能接受那些你认为不好的信念影响，比如说原罪的负面暗示等。然而，没有一个人在那方面是没有任何一种信念的，的确，无神论的信念也是一种信念。", "en": "It may seem that your religious beliefs have little to do with your health or with your day-to-day experience. Those of you who have left organized religions may feel relatively free from what you consider to be the adverse connotations of original sin and the like. Yet no one is free of belief of any kind in that area. Indeed, a belief in atheism is a belief.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第646节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "646", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0812", "zh": "如果你自觉萎靡，而恰好读到关于维生素的广告或书本，而被它所影响，那么你的确会受益至少有那么一阵子。你的信念会让维生素对你生效，但如果你坚持健康不好的状况会持续的话，那么维生素所代表的相反暗示也不会长期有效的。", "en": "If you are feeling poorly and happen to read an advertisement for vitamins, or a book about them, and are impressed, you will indeed benefit — at least for a while. Your belief will make them work for you, but if your insistence upon poor health persists, then the counter suggestion represented by the vitamins will not be effective for long.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第660节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "660", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0907", "zh": "梦里生活有个层面是特定地为了处理身体的生物状况的，不只是给你有关健康问题的暗示，并且给你它们的理由，以及解决它们的方法。关于可能的未来的信息也给了你，以助你做有意识的抉择。可是，你已教给你自己，你不可能在梦中有意识，因为你如此诠释「有意识」这字，以致它只是指出你自己有成见的概念。结果是，你们没有任何文化上可被接受的模式，允许你能更好的利用你的梦（As a result, you do not have any culturally acceptable patterns that allow you to use your dreams competently.）。", "en": "One level of dream life deals particularly with the biological condition of the body, giving you not just hints of health difficulties, but the reasons for them and the ways to circumvent them. Information about the probable future is also given to help you make conscious choices. You have taught yourselves that you cannot be conscious in your dreams, however, because you interpret the word “conscious” so that it indicates only your own prejudiced concept. As a result, you do not have any culturally acceptable patterns that allow you to use your dreams competently.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第763节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "763", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0962", "zh": "（在此时，不赞成这种手术的必要性的医生比赞成要多得多。那些反对这种手术的人，说到在诊断里的可能错误，包括对那个“乳房X光摄影”图形的误诊。再次的，负面的暗示主宰了现在，而被投射到将来，因为这个人被告以，她是在她自己随时会出差错的身体机能的掌握之下。", "en": "At this time many more doctors disagree than agree with the need for prophylactic mastectomies. Those against the procedure cite the errors possible in diagnosis, including the misinterpretation of mammographic patterns. Once again, negative suggestion rules in the present and is projected into the future, for the individual is told that she is at the mercy of her own bodily processes, which might go awry at any moment.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第805节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "805", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1021", "zh": "可是，如你所知，保护的概念本身就暗示了威胁——所以，如果你相信威胁，你最好要有保护。鲁柏没有必要再看见那形相——只要感觉那有力的能量之实相，并且了解它是替他做事的就够了。以一种方式，那形相也代表了天真及有力的内我、自发的自己或自然的神奇自己——这些都是同义词。", "en": "The very idea of protection, however, as you know, implies a threat—so if you believe in threats you had better have protection. It was not necessary for Ruburt to see the form again—merely to sense the reality of that powerful energy, and realize that it worked on his behalf. In a fashion the form also represented the innocent and powerful inner self, or spontaneous self, or naturally magical self—the terms are synonymous.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第922节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "922", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e1060", "zh": "趁空来访。她曾受过伤，当她跌倒而扭到或拉到腿里的钢钉时，她又复发了。现在医生预告她将有很长的一段复原期。当她跟我们聊天时，珍和我很快便注意到她医师给过她的负面暗示。她也告诉我们，另一位护士将因背部扭痛而至少请假一个礼拜，显然是她在试图抬起一位病人时受的伤。这使我们对于在医院里工作有所好奇——仿佛每个人迟早都会得病。", "en": "(One of the nurse’s aides stopped by for a visit. She had been injured and suffered a relapse when she fell and twisted or pulled on some of the staples in her leg. Now a prolonged recovery period is predicted. Jane and I soon noticed the negative suggestions her doctor had given her, as she talked with us. She also told us that another nurse will be out for at least a week with a strained back, which she evidently got from trying to lift a patient. It made us wonder about working in hospitals — it seemed everyone was sick at one time or another.", "source": "健康之道 · 第1节", "year": "1984", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "健康之道", "session": "1", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "怎么给自己下暗示：一套能上手的配方", "note": "AI总结：赛斯给的不是玄法，是操作说明。睡前是黄金时段：恰当的睡前暗示能保证身体完全恢复，两段三小时的睡眠就够了；每晚的暗示应放在整体健康与活力上，并且带着对第二天活动的预期画面。想做出体，就告诉自己：你想记得，一如你想投射——想象那股上升的感觉，告诉自己身体睡着时你的有一部分会保持警醒，甚至暗示自己投射后马上醒来把经验写下。暗示自动建立起调整，而且几乎是立即生效，还会给修复过程加速。它也不止以你想的方式回应：这些建议会以无数方式出现——身体可能自己开始渴望某种食物、新鲜空气或运动。连自我对话的语气都有讲究：把不信任的感受当成自己疼爱的、被吓怕的部分，同情地对它说话，告诉它为什么不必再怕——这样的建议付诸实行，价值可观；轻度的忧虑、紧张、健康不良同样用得上。判断：配方人人能试，核心动作是把「热切相信」重复到不用再检查。", "src": "第 7、11、295、325、462、481、501、532、632 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 7 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 11 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 295 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 325 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 462 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 481 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 501 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 532 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 632 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0456", "zh": "这些建议自动产生调整，而且，你会注意到，几乎是立即有效。在脚部的状况中，肌肉一直被误用，它们需要一阵子才会完全修复。无论如何，这些建议将会加速此一过程。立刻治愈是可能的，但他现在还不到那个时候。", "en": "The recommendations automatically set up readjustments, and, you will note, almost instantly. In the case of the foot the muscles have been misused and will take a while to completely repair themselves. Suggestion however will speed the process. An instant cure is possible, but he is not at that point.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第295节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "295", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0498", "zh": "现在重新尝试投射，对他非常有利。就工作而言，他的热情正在回升。这会自动产生助益。每天晚上的暗示现在应该就在整体健康和活力上，而且要有第二天活动的预期画面。", "en": "00f His enthusiasm is returning as far as his work is concerned. This is automatically beneficial. Nightly suggestions should deal now with general health and vitality, and with pictures of anticipation for the following day’s activities.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第325节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "325", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0508", "zh": "暗示你投射后马上醒来，把经验写下来，是非常有益的。这有助于它从其他梦经验分隔开来，并且提醒你。你当然需要考虑睡眠，但这种方法是最好的一个。", "en": "It is quite beneficial to suggest you will awake at once afterward, to write the experience down. This helps to isolate it from other dream experience, and to alert you. You have sleep to consider of course, but this method is the best one of all.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第325节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "325", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0629", "zh": "我帮了你，而你投射出去了。告诉你自己：你想记得，一如你想投射。甚至可以想象那股上升的感觉——当我助你出去的时候。这些都在你入睡时做。其他暗示：告诉你自己，当你的身体睡着时，你的有一部分会保持警醒。", "en": "I helped you, and you projected. Tell yourself that you want to remember as much as you want to project. Even imagine the rising sensationsas I help you out. This as you fall to sleep. Other suggestions: tell yourself that a portion of you will remain alert while your body sleeps.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第462节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "462", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0643", "zh": "如果你们要从梦的状态里做起，那么你们必须留出两个半小时，因为头一段会被当作预备工作用掉。你们也可以在睡前给自己这样的暗示。你们不妨先约定彼此见面的时间与地点，比方说凌晨三点在客厅。", "en": "If you try to do this from a dream state then you must set aside two and one-half hours, for the first portion will be used as preliminaries. You can also give yourselves such suggestions before you sleep. You might begin by making an appointment to meet each other, say at three in the morning in the living room.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第481节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "481", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0685", "zh": "现在：到了此刻，你完全可能造访这间屋子。给自己那个暗示。", "en": "Now: it is quite possible for you at this point now to visit this room. Give yourself the suggestion.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第501节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "501", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0754", "zh": "对大多数人来说，两段三小时一次的睡眠相当足够了，但是在睡前要给自己恰当的建议，这种暗示能使身体得以完全恢复。十小时的睡眠往往反而对身体不利，比如说：会使身心变得呆滞不振等等。睡眠时“精神离体太久，使肌肉丧失弹性。”（珍说得相当快，而且整节课如此）", "en": "Two periods of three hours apiece would be quite sufficient for most people, if the proper suggestions were given before sleep — suggestions that would insure the body’s complete recuperation. In many cases ten hours sleep, for example, is actually disadvantageous, resulting in a sluggishness both of mind and body. In this case the spirit has simply been away from the body for too long a time, resulting in a loss of muscular flexibility. (Jane’s delivery was quite fast, and remained so throughout the session.)", "source": "时空之外 · 第532节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "532", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0780", "zh": "这些建议将以无数的方式出现——有些以你们的思想方式来说是相当实质的，有些则借其他方法，例如，身体本身可能开始渴望某种食物，或新鲜空气，或运动。这些是简单的例子，以后我们将会更明确些。", "en": "These suggestions will appear in numberless ways — some quite physical to your way of thinking, and some through other means. The body may of itself begin to crave certain foods, for example, or fresh air or exercise. These are simple instances, and later we will be more specific.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第632节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "632", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1112", "zh": "实际上，鲁柏该同情地对待那些感受，解释给它们听，它们来自何方。这容许那情绪一些清晰的解决。他甚至可能视那些不信任的感觉为：他自己疼爱的、被吓怕的部分，然后，再次的，同情地对自己的那个部分说话——告诉它，它为什么不必再害怕，而在言词和情绪上强调，自己被吓怕的部分现在不再需要防御，却能允许它自己自由和自然的表达。这些建议，如果付诸实行的话，其价值会是相当可观的。告诉鲁柏，在我们的下一节，我将再开始书的口授。包括谈“越来越好的药”的资料。", "en": "Ruburt should actually address those feelings sympathetically, explaining to them where they came from. This allows the emotions some clear resolution. He may even refer to those feelings of distrust as a dear frightened part of himself, and then, again, address that part of the self sympathetically — telling it why it need no longer be frightened, and vocally and emotionally stressing the fact that the frightened portion of the self no longer needs defenses, but can now allow itself free and natural expression. These suggestions, carried out, can be of more than considerable value. Tell Ruburt I will begin book dictation again at our next session, including the material on “better and better pills.”", "source": "健康之道 · 第7节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "7", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1122", "zh": "在这儿给的所有建议，于较轻的状况里也有帮助——在平常发作的忧虑、紧张或健康不良里。即使那些有非常严重疾病的人，也永远能希望有所改进，因此，即使一个人由于一个严重的健康难局而考虑自杀，这事也该被慎重的权衡。", "en": "All of the suggestions given here will also help in lesser situations, in ordinary bouts of worry, stress, or poor health. Even those with very serious diseases can always hope for improvement, so even if an individual is considering suicide because of a severe health dilemma, the matter should be carefully weighed.", "source": "健康之道 · 第11节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "11", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "他们自己天天在用：珍和罗的实验记录", "note": "AI总结：这块全是罗的笔记，说明暗示不是赛斯的理论摆设，而是这对夫妻的日常工具。珍在上定期课之前给自己下正面暗示；罗暗示自己「感觉轻盈」来做出体实验，震颤感随暗示而至；他用暗示希望再次发生某种接触；他睡前提示自己记得梦并写下来；他也试着用暗示做投射。赛斯给的暗示被罗用在生活中——按建议有意识地改进对父母的反应，结果非常好。暗示也会被潜意识「照字面执行」：珍在第一次自我警报后下了放慢速度的暗示，结果实验结束许久征象才显现——她怀疑正是那句暗示被过度当真了。赛斯还试图教房东太太正面暗示，用在一颗良性肿瘤上；珍按赛斯谈疗愈梦的内容给自己下暗示，随后小睡里果然做了长而逼真的疗愈梦；晚期他们甚至把建议录音给珍每天听，用来鼓励架构二的活动。判断：这条脉络最有说服力的地方是——他们把暗示当实验做，并记录成败。", "src": "第 36、54、103、199、220、243、248、541、583、939 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 36 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 54 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 103 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 199 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 220 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 243 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 248 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 541 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 583 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 939 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0039", "zh": "（今晚，比尔·麦唐纳，将作为我们的第一个正式见证者，预定要完整出席课程。我和珍都发现，我们有很高的兴致，期待着这个事件的到来。晚上8:00。珍躺下休息了一会，并给自己一些有关这一节的正面暗示。比尔预定8:30到达。", "en": "（Tonight our first formal witness, Bill Macdonnel, was to attend a full session. Jane and I found ourselves anticipating the event with a good deal of interest. At 8:00 PM. Jane lay down for a rest, and gave herself positive suggestions concerning the session. Bill was due at 8:30.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0057", "zh": "（5月20日，星期三，晚上8:20 ：在这一节，在第55节上课之前，已经没有太多时间。我有很多震颤感的例子。第一次很强烈出现在我暗示自己感觉很轻盈的时候；然后它就袭向我，同一时间，我的左臂感觉特别轻，几乎没有重量。", "en": "（Wednesday, May 20, 8:20 PM: There was not much time before the session, the 55th, was due. I had many examples of my thrilling sensation. The first time quite strongly appeared when I suggested to myself that I felt light; then it washed over me, and at the same time my arms particularly felt very light, almost weightless.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0146", "zh": "（珍怀疑在第一次自我警报响了之后，她下了放慢速度的暗示，实际上是她的潜意识所做的解读；因此后来在她的实验“结束”好一阵子之后，征象才显现。这主要是她的想法，不是我的。", "en": "（Jane was also correct in suspecting that her suggestion to go slowly, after her first ego-alarm, was literally interpreted by her subconscious; hence the later manifestation of symptoms quite a while after her experiment had “ended.” This was much more her idea than mine.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第103节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "103", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0319", "zh": "（珍在今晚上8点时表示，她不介意我们是否会有信封测试。我谈到这将会是忙碌的一节课，有加拉格夫妇和殷斯翠姆博士的资料，有可能做信封测试，有机会的话，赛斯也可能谈谈珍在上星期五早上小睡时做的两个非常长、逼真而且难懂的梦，详情请看珍在第四册第198节的描述。她相信其中至少有一个梦是疗愈梦，因为她在上节赛斯谈到疗愈梦之后给自己下了暗示。", "en": "（Jane said at 8 PM this evening that she did not mind if we had an envelope test. I remarked that it was going to be a busy session, what with the material on the Gallaghers and Dr. Instream, a possible envelope test, and the chance that Seth might discuss two very long, vivid, and complicated dreams Jane had while taking a short nap last Friday morning. See Jane's account in Volume 4, on pages 336. 38. She believes that at least one of these dreams is a therapeutic dream, resulting from suggestions she gave herself following Seth's material on therapeutic dreams in the last session.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第199节", "year": "1966", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "199", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0360", "zh": "（我有很多次希望能有另一次这样的接触，我承诺自己，下次会做得更好。虽然不是每晚，我也用了暗示，希望这样的经验能再发生。目前还没有什么进展。）", "en": "（I have hoped many times for another such contact, with the promise to myself that I would do better next time. I have also used suggestion, although not nightly, to the effect that more such experiences would occur. Nothing has developed to date.）", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第220节", "year": "1966", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "220", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0399", "zh": "（上周日，1966年3月20日，珍和我去宾州塞尔市我父母的家中探望他们。我们相处愉快。按照赛斯最近的建议——他通常是在临时课给出这类建议——我一直有意识地努力改进我对我父母的反应。结果非常好。）", "en": "（Jane and I visited my parents at their home in Sayre, PA, last Sunday, March 20,1966. We got along well. Following Seth’s recent suggestions, usually given in unscheduled sessions, I have been making conscious efforts concerning my reactions to my parents. The results have been very good.）", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第243节", "year": "1967", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "243", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0415", "zh": "（见第247节。赛斯试图指导我们的房东太太玛丽安·史帕日尼做正面暗示，也教她如何把它应用在一颗良性卵巢肿瘤上。", "en": "（See the 247th session. In it Seth attempted to instruct our landlady Marian Spaziani, regarding positive suggestion and its application to a benign ovarian tumor.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第248节", "year": "1967", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "248", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0714", "zh": "（今天下午，当我躺下时我给自己建议要有个投射经验，但没成功。然后，晚餐后不久，我有了一次像第八章第534节的课中所描写的视觉干扰。当它在进行时我告诉了珍。她又一次觉得很担心，但我却照旧地不觉惊慌。这情形持续了约半小时。", "en": "(This afternoon, I gave myself suggestions that I have a projection experience when I lay down, but I did not succeed. Then, shortly after supper, I had a visual experience like that described in the notes for the 534th session, in Chapter Eight. I told Jane about it as it progressed. Once again she was concerned, but as usual I felt no alarm. The experience lasted for perhaps half an hour.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第541节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "541", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0746", "zh": "（昨晚，星期二，当珍在客厅上ESP课时我去睡了。那时差不多是十一点三十分。在我躺着假寐时，我提示自己在早晨我会记得我的梦而把它写下来。够奇怪的，我并没有提及“灵体投射”。", "en": "(Last night, Tuesday, I went to bed while Jane was holding ESP class in the living room. It was about 11:30. As I lay dozing I gave myself suggestions that I would recall my dreams in the morning and write them down. Oddly enough, I didn’t mention “astral projection.”", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第583节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "583", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1035", "zh": "（我们讨论赛斯资料以及我们自己想法的这个计划——包括每天给珍听我们录下来的建议——是来自十二月一日及三日的那些课。显然，我们正试着鼓励架构二的活动。“罗和赛斯给我们开始了一个计划，虽然我们几乎还没开始，但我真的感到一点轻松及平静。”这是五日早上当珍坐在新矮桌旁时的一部分打字。“昨天我觉得这个地方在我周围滴答作响。下午我回了一点信，但并没真的开始写那原为计划一部分的笔记。我的打字仍然很糟，但我知道这会改进。在这些杂记里，我不觉得有任何灵感之流，但我的确感觉到一个潜在的流在浮出。而且我真的觉得……稳定，比较满足……当我写到这儿时，我感觉有一个明确的表达阻碍，以及一些不太严重的恐慌，但认知到当我决定写杂记时有一种压抑的感觉这事实……立刻写下来，我将告诉罗。”", "en": "However, she did not type the summary I’d asked her for. That evening she held the second of the four private sessions she was to give before starting Chapter 12 of Dreams.3 Our program of discussing Seth’s material, as well as our own ideas—which included our taping suggestions for Jane to listen to daily—had come out of those sessions for December 1 and 3. Obviously, we were trying to encourage Framework 2 activity. I spent the next day rearranging all of Jane’s working paraphernalia in her writing room, following her directions, and that re-creation of her world helped also. “Rob and Seth started us on a new program and though we’ve hardly begun, I do feel some relieved more peaceful,” she typed in part on the morning of the 5th as she sat at her new low table, “yesterday i felt the place clicking about me. P.M. I did a little mail but didn’t really get into the notes which are to be a part of the program. My typing is still pretty poor but do know this will improve. I don’t feel any flow in these notes but I do feel a submerged flow rising and i do feel… centered, more content… as I get this far I feel a definite block of expression and some mild enough panic but recognize the fact that a feeling of repression came as I decided to do my notes… writing down at once and will tell rob.”", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第939节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": "罗的笔记", "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "939", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "暗示的用武之地：睡眠、梦、出体、疗愈与日常", "note": "AI总结：赛斯的建议覆盖面很宽，从大毛病到小习惯。健康上：一套完整的操作说明涵盖饮食（少酱汁、新鲜蔬果、冷冻好过罐头）与作息（每天短促散步这种看似微不足道的建议其实非常有益）；对控制症状，珍还远远没用足暗示这个工具，而照着做就能把人带回正轨。心灵能力上：认识全我的其他中心可以借潜意识层面的暗示做到；好方法能让你带着醒时意识同行，睡时意识不再因害怕而掐断经验；鲁柏在潜意识基础上暗示了自己的漂浮梦，成效极佳；他的诗集则是「暗示如何为意识的目的运用能量」的绝佳例子。氛围也算数：卧室里一盏灯、一件睡袍放置的位置，都带着隐含的暗示之意，负面暗示的氛围要特别留意；连摆锤都能用来发掘并改变潜意识的感受——正负两种暗示都在象征层面起作用。判断：暗示不是专用武器，是环境、身体、梦境通吃的基础操作。", "src": "第 1、151、178、185、228、235、261、281、318、336、400 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 1 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 178 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 185 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 228 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 235 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 261 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 281 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 318 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 336 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 400 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0176", "zh": "约瑟，我相信我应该再一次建议你，每天短暂散步一会儿，这样的建议也许看起来微不足道，但其实不然，而且事实会证明非常有益。在享受自然之时，的确有一种价值完成，可以让你从许多束缚中得到解脱。", "en": "I believe I should once again suggest, Joseph, a daily short walk for you. Such suggestions may appear trivial, yet they are not, and will prove most beneficial. There is indeed a value fulfillment within the enjoyment of nature that can release you from many restraints.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0257", "zh": "他的书在各方面都会很成功，而且陆续会有其他类的书。在潜意识的基础上，鲁柏实际上已暗示了他最近的漂浮梦，而且也获得极佳的成效。他对自己的能力不够有信心，从这个观点来说，漂浮梦的成功对他帮助最大。", "en": "His book will be successful in many ways, and there will be other such books. On a subconscious basis Ruburt actually suggested his recent levitation dreams, with most effective results. He was not confident enough of his own abilities, and the dream success was most beneficial from this viewpoint.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第178节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "178", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0278", "zh": "我会给你们建议，也会告诉你们这些建议背后的理由。我还要谈一些饮食控制的问题。你们目前做得还不错，不会加太多的调味料和酱汁。这边不用怕必要的维生素会摄取不够，我主要是建议食物的烹调方式要改变，尽量食用新鲜蔬果，冷冻的比罐头好。", "en": "I will give you the suggestions, and then I will give you the reasons behind them. I will have some little more to say concerning diet. You do well as it is, avoiding thick sauces and gravies. There is no fear here of short-circuiting necessary vitamin needs. I am mainly suggesting a change in the way food is prepared, and whenever possible a reliance upon fresh vegetables and fruits. Frozen are preferable to canned.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第185节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "185", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0371", "zh": "然后我要简短地说一下关于鲁柏的诗集，因为这是一个绝佳的例子，关于暗示是如何为了意识的目的来运用能量。", "en": "Then I will speak briefly concerning Ruburts book of poetry, for this is an excellent example of how suggestion can be used to utilize energy for conscious purposes.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第228节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "228", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0381", "zh": "全我的每一层，或每一个部分，都想像它是意识的中心，而这个全我绕着它旋转。目前为止，你对这些其他的“中心”有着很少的经验——你可以把它放在括号里——但很快地我们会给你一些概念，而让你至少对此变得有点熟悉。一开始这可以借由潜意识层面的暗示而做到。", "en": "Each layer, or each area of the whole self, imagines that it is the center of awareness, and that the whole self revolves about it. So far you have had little experience with these other “centers”—you may put that in quotation marks—but before too long we shall give you some ideas so that you may become at least slightly acquainted. Initially this will be done through suggestion on a subconscious level.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第235节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "235", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0422", "zh": "现在。福克斯的一些建议非常好。它们会让你带着醒时意识与你同行。在你发展能力而且越来越习惯这个经验时，醒时意识就会记得越来越多，而不会害怕。当它害怕时，你看，它会迫使整体经验就此结束。如果不带着恐惧，同样的经验可能会继续下去，而让全我获得更大的利益。", "en": "Now. Some of Fox’s suggestions are excellent. They will allow you to take the waking consciousness along with you. As your abilities develop and as you become more accustomed to the experience, the waking consciousness will recall more and more, and not become frightened. When it becomes frightened you see it forces the whole experience to end. If it were not taken along the same experience might have continued, and greater benefits been achieved for the whole self.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第261节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "261", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0446", "zh": "发掘你的潜意识有何感觉，摆锤是一个绝佳的方法，而不是改变它们。顺便说一下，如你们两人所知，从几个观点看来，你今天晚上播放的音乐非常有益（伊玛·苏马克[Yma Sumac]）。与过去充满生产力或喜悦的时期有关的任何连结，都和当下有直接的关系。就像负面的暗示有它们的作用一样，正面的暗示也是，而且两者都是就象征而言。", "en": "The pendulum is an excellent method of discovering your subconscious feelings, and indeed of changing them. As you both suppose, incidentally, the music you played this evening was highly beneficial from several standpoints. (Yma Sumac.) Any connection with past periods of productivity or joy have immediate reference to the present. As negative suggestions play their part, so do positive suggestions, and both in terms of symbols.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第281节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "281", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0477", "zh": "顺便说一下，卧室里的一盏小台灯让他更不愿意在那里睡觉。粉红色的睡袍应该暂时不要和毛衣摆放在一起。事实上，可能应该把它扔了，因为卧室隐含的暗示之意。（停顿）", "en": "The small lamp in the bedroom, incidentally, added to his disinclination to sleep there. The pink nightgown should be lain away with the sweaters for now. In fact it should probably be disposed of, because of the bedroom connotation. (Pause.)", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第318节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "318", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0519", "zh": "我们的耶稣会士发现，从潜意识层面来说，自发的投射对纾解压力最有益处。平心而论，他的确跨出了一大步，这种状况发生的频率，远比他所了解的还多。然而，他尚未充分利用暗示来协助自己控制症状。", "en": "Now. Our Jesuit finds spontaneous projections most beneficial on a subconscious level, to relieve pressure. Quite literally he does indeed step out of himself. This happens much more frequently than he realizes. He has not utilized suggestion, however, to any significant degree as an aid in controlling his symptoms.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第336节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "336", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0565", "zh": "他已经觉得需要睡眠，因为他太急着想把事情搞定，遵循这些建议可以使他回到正轨。我现在可以告诉他这类的事情，而在几个月前，他不准我说，后来症状复发。我们正在走捷径处理所有问题。", "en": "He has felt the need of sleep because he has been overly anxious to set things right. These suggestions, followed, will return him to his proper course. I am able to tell him such things now. Months ago he would not have allowed me to speak until he had a return of symptoms. We are short-circuiting all of that now.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第400节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "400", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "几个常被问反的问题：会被暗示绑架吗", "note": "AI总结：早期课里赛斯就把边界讲清楚了：珍在出神状态下传述，这种束缚不会比自我暗示更严重——那是她同意的现象，一瞬间就能把意识注意力转回物质环境。所以「暗示控制论」不成立：没有人会不管愿不愿意地被负面暗示动摇，每个人都有一整团的信念和暗示，那些东西相当字面地反映在肉体本身上。由此推出几条实用原则：当你对某事有期望时，方法自然来，但信心必须端出来；在催眠测体温这类实验里，关于结果应该怎样的暗示反而会模糊那个效果——观察者别用自己的暗示污染实验；连「令人讨厌的食物」都是暗示点，逆转过程一旦开始，人格朝健康前进，接着就会看到看似奇迹的康复。最重要的一条是自由：没有一条路被不可挽回地设定，没有任何行动固定到无法改变——这正是暗示能起作用的前提。甚至「母亲特质与性伴侣特质对立」这类矛盾感，也只是被你暗示出来的错觉。判断：暗示的方向盘始终在你手里，问题只是你有没有意识到自己在握着它。", "src": "第 16、28、77、212、347、658、704、735 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 16 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 28 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 77 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 212 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 347 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 658 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 704 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 735 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0007", "zh": "（一开始，不必过于仔细检验资料；也就是说，首先变成物质化，否则没有什么可以检验。暗示是一种很好的手段。镜子对我来说是个辅助，在一个平的层面看到透视。罗问到早前我出现有关“草原”的那句话是怎么回事（注：即上文“不曾有风吹过草原，但我就在那里”），马尔巴说，那时她正在试图接触我们。她在前世与我们没有任何关联，只是可以接触而已。有时在她的层面，除非他们觉得与寻求接触的人合得来，否则他们不会回应而把管道打开。", "en": "（Don’t worry about checking data so carefully to begin with; that is, get materializations first or you won’t have anything to check. Suggestion is a good tool. Mirror is a help to me, see perspective on a flat plane. Rob asked about prairie quote earlier, Malba said she was trying to make contact. She is not related to us in any way in a past life, just was available. Sometimes they will not respond on her plane to open channels unless they feel compatible with people seeking contact.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第16节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "16", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0026", "zh": "我的确依赖鲁柏的解离意愿。无疑，有时在课间他对周围环境一无所知。但是，这对他的束缚不会比自我暗示更严重。这个现象是经过他同意的，任何时候，只要一瞬间，他就可以把意识的注意力转回到物质环境上。", "en": "I do depend upon Ruburt’s willingness to dissociate. There is no doubt that at times he is unaware of his surroundings during a session. However, this is no more binding upon him than autosuggestion. It is a phenomena in which he gives consent, and he could, at any time and in a split second, return his conscious attention upon the physical environment.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0102", "zh": "我知道你们将会对我接下来的这个建议提出异议，基于你们自认为实际的理由。不过，由于你们的特别体质，这种小型假期应该要成为你们每年生活中的一部分；当你们对它们有期望时，方法自然来。但一定要有信心。", "en": "I know that this next suggestion will meet protests on both of your parts, for what you suppose to be practical reasons. Nevertheless, because of your particular constitutions, small vacations should definitely become a part of your yearly existence; and when you expect them, the means for them will come. But faith must be shown.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第77节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "77", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0350", "zh": "不过我应该指出，除了一些其他情况是例外，潜意识的不同层次会落在明确的温度范围。到某些程度这事实可以透过催眠弄清楚。不过，关于受测者体温应该是上升或下降的效果暗示可能会模糊了这个效果。", "en": "It should be noted however, that with the exception of several other circumstances the various levels of the subconscious can be found to fall within definite temperature ranges. To some extent this fact can be ascertained through hypnosis. However, suggestion as to the effect that the subjects temperature should rise or fall would tend to obscure the effect.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第212节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "212", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0542", "zh": "暗示点开始自我消散，你们预期的活动会进一步加速它们消散。你知道，令人讨厌的食物就是暗示点，一旦逆转过程开始，人格也朝向健康前进，接着过程中就会看到明显康复的现象。", "en": "The cue points began to break up of themselves, and your anticipated activities will further aid in their deterioration. The offending foods were cue points, you see. Once the reversal process has begun and the personality swung back toward health, then the process shows what seems to be remarkable recovery.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第347节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "347", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0801", "zh": "你们有些人只是精神怠惰，而不去有意识地检查自己收到的资料。许多人惯于“否定”由别人那儿来的负面建议，反之，拼命去维护正面的肯定信念，实际上，这样做是因为他们完全地信服负面信念的力量比有益的那些要强。", "en": "Some of you are simply mentally lazy. You do not consciously examine the data that you receive. Many who make a practice of “denying” negative suggestions from others, asserting positive affirmations instead, actually do so because they are so fully convinced that the power of negative beliefs is stronger than that of beneficial ones.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第658节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "658", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0852", "zh": "在这儿其全面的实际暗示应该被了解：没有一条路是不可挽回地被设定或已无法改变的。不过，在你们通常运作的有限架构之内是可以做出所谓的预言的，而且到某个程度，它们也将会成立，可是，以更深的说法，没有一个行动是固定而无法改变的。未知的实相是已知实相的源头；如果你想“发现”事情是如何运作的话，那么，你的旅程终究必须引你进入隐于你所知世界之内的次元。", "en": "The full practical implication here should be understood: No course is irrevocably set or beyond change. Within the limited framework of your usual operations, however, so-called predictions3 may be made. They will be workable to some degree. In deeper terms however no action is set beyond alteration. The unknown reality is the source for the known one. If you want to “discover” how things work, then your journey must eventually lead you into the dimensions that lie within the world you know.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第704节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "704", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0882", "zh": "有时候你表现得好像一个能力抵触了另一个似的，你想：“我无法作一个好父母，而同时又是我配偶的一个性伴侣。”对那些这么想的人这可能暗示了一个必然的矛盾。一个女人也许觉得母亲的特质几乎与充满活力的性伴侣之特质直接对立。一个男人可能想象父职意味着提供一个非常好的房子与收入。他也许认为“攻击性”、竞争性与情感上的冷漠是扮演好那个角色所必须的，而这可能被认为是与一个丈夫所“必备”的爱、了解与情感上的支持这些特质是对立的，当然，实际上，这种对立全部没有必要。 可是以同样的方式，你常常仿佛觉得你的身份是依赖着某个非常明确的角色，直到那些也是你自己的特质看来仿佛颇具威胁性。它们看起来几乎像是“非自己”似的。", "en": "Sometimes you act as though one ability contradicts another. You think “I cannot be a good parent and a sexual partner to my mate at the same time.” To those who feel this way a definite contradiction seems implied. A woman might feel that the qualities of a mother almost stand in opposition to those of an exuberant sex mate. A man might imagine that fatherhood meant providing an excellent home and income. He might think that “aggressiveness,”6 competition, and emotional aloofness were required to perform that role. These would be considered in opposition to the qualities of love, understanding, and emotional support “required” of a husband. In actuality, of course, no such contradictions apply. In the same way, however, you often seem to feel that your identity is dependent upon a certain highly specific role, until other qualities quite your own seem threatening. They almost seem to be unselflike.7", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第735节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "735", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "另一层意思：每句话底下都没说完的部分", "note": "AI总结：「暗示」在赛斯语料里还有第二个用法，跟下指令无关，而是指「明说底下暗含的东西」——而且这一层被他抬到了形而上的高度。语言的意义只因为它骑在无声的节奏上：标点是你听不见的声音，一个停顿暗示了未放出的声音的存在；你的肉体生命同样暗示了一个非肉体的源头——那被暗示的、未言明的、未物质化的活力，供给了肉体分子的字母成分。往上推：物质世界暗示了一个神的世界，神的存在也暗示物质世界的存在；实质事件暗示了基本上非实质的力量组成的心理组织，那些被选中的可能事件在侧翼等待实质实现。集体层面同理：一场具体的群体事件，暗示了一个会让你们科技通信系统相形见绌的内在沟通网；战争则是透过集体暗示、动用国家资源完成的集体自杀——执行者深信宇宙不安全、陌生人有敌意。连时间都如此：未来对现在的暗示（预知性的反应）与对过去事件的反应同样真实。判断：学会读「没说的部分」，是读赛斯乃至读世界的基本功——所有显现的东西都暗示着它的来处。", "src": "第 4、8、13、719、776、780、781、789、818、822、835、881 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 4 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 8 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 13 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 719 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 776 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 780 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 781 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 789 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 818 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 822 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 835 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 881 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e0865", "zh": "如果你平常能够处理物质实相的话，你就不会在意识的转换里或在离开你的本台时遭遇困难。不过，照道理来讲：如果你在纽约市有问题的话，不论你旅行到那里去，你也极可能以一种不同的形式碰到它们。经由改变你通常的取向，换个环境也许会帮助你头脑清楚些，因此，你能更清楚的看到你你自己而获益。当你离开你的本台时，这也同样适用，在此，可能的利益远比在通常的生活与旅行里大得多，但你仍是你自己。不以某种方式去建构实相是不可能的。实相暗示了一个结构。", "en": "If you are normally capable of dealing with physical reality, you will encounter no difficulties in alterations of consciousness, or leaving your home station. Be reasonable, however: If you have difficulties in New York City, you are most apt to encounter them in a different form no matter where else you might travel. A change of environment might help clear your head by altering your usual orientation, so that you can see yourself more clearly, and benefit. The same applies when you leave your home station. Here the possible benefits are far greater than in usual life and travel, but you are still yourself. It is impossible not to structure reality in some fashion. Reality implies a structuring.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第719节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "719", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0914", "zh": "到某程度，标点是你们听不见的声音一个停顿，暗示了一个未放出的声音的在场。你们，到某种程度，语言依赖未说的部分就如依赖已说的部分，而和依赖无声的节奏与依赖声音一样。不过，在那范围，无声只涉及声音的停顿，在其中被暗示了声音但未被放出。内在的声音主要是处理那种关系。语言的有意义只因它驾于其上的无声节奏（Language is meaningful only because of the rhythm of the silence upon which it rides）。", "en": "To some extent punctuation is sound that you do not hear, a pause that implies the presence of withheld sound. To some extent, then, language is as dependent upon the unspoken as the spoken, and the rhythm of silence as well as of sound. In that context, however, silence involves merely a pause of sound in which sound is implied but withheld. Inner sound deals primarily with that kind of relationship. Language is meaningful only because of the rhythm of the silence upon which it rides.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第776节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "776", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0921", "zh": "那么，你肉体本身的生命就暗示了一个「源头」，一个肉体生命自其中冒出的生命——这被暗示的、未言明的、未物质化的、无声的活力，供给了实相的、肉体的分子的「字母」成分（Your very physical life, then, implies a “source,” a life out of which the physical one emerges, dash — the implied, unspoken, unmaterialized, unsounded vitality that supplied the ingredients for the physical, bodily, molecular “alphabet.”）。因此，你的肉体生命，暗示了一个非肉体的生命。你把你的特定「语言」如此视为当然，而如此不费力的用它，以致你想都没想它暗示了其它的语言或它获得其意义是因为从未说出的内在假设，或由于运用了在其间没有发出声音的停顿的这个事实。你也以相同的方式过你的生活。", "en": "Your very physical life, then, implies a “source,” a life out of which the physical one emerges, dash — the implied, unspoken, unmaterialized, unsounded vitality that supplied the ingredients for the physical, bodily, molecular “alphabet.” Your physical life therefore implies a nonphysical one. You take your particular “language” so for granted, and use it so effortlessly, that you give no thought at all to the fact that it implies other languages also, or that it gains its meaning because of inner assumptions that are never spoken, or by the use of pauses in which no sounds are made. You live your lives in the same fashion.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第780节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "780", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0928", "zh": "物质世界就暗示了一个神的世界。神的存在也暗示了一个物质世界的存在。", "en": "The physical world implies the existence of a god. God’s existence also implies the existence of a physical world.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第781节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "781", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0935", "zh": "实质事件暗示了基本上非实质的力量集合成为一个组织，这组织原本是存在于时空范畴之外的。这是一个心理的组织，包含一组被选择的可能事件。可以这么说，这些在侧翼等待着实质地实现。那实现的最终发动也可来自醒时或梦中状态，但它代表所需的最后因素——灵感、欲望或目的之加快——那将突然地发动原本的心理组织，而成为实质的发生。", "en": "Physical events imply the collection of basically nonphysical forces into an organization that exists initially outside of the time-space context. This is a psychological organization, consisting of a selection of chosen probable events. These wait in the wings, so to speak, for physical actualization. The final trigger for that actualization may come from the waking or dream states, but it will represent the final factor needed — the quickening of inspiration, desire, or purpose — that will suddenly activate the initial psychological organization as a physical occurrence.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第789节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "789", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0969", "zh": "在你们的世界里，知识必须被转译为明确的细节，但我们也在处理那些无法如此容易的解读的情感实相。在这节当中，在我说出的字句里——但更重要的，在这节的气氛里——暗示了那些无法解读却有力的实相，然后在你们的时间里，那些实相将渐渐的以你们能懂的字语被描写出来。", "en": "In your world knowledge must be translated into specifics, yet we also deal with emotional realities that cannot be so easily deciphered. In this session, in the words I speak — but more importantly in the atmosphere of the session — there are hints of those undecipherable yet powerful realities that will then, in your time, gradually be described in verbal terms that make sense to you.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第818节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "818", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0975", "zh": "如果你想改变工作，而心怀那个欲望，一个新的工作就会以完全同样的方式进入你的经验，因为内在事件会由内我来安排。一件身体上的事件涉及了许多肌肉关节等等的作用。就如涉及工作改变的一个事件也关系到许多人的动作，并且暗示了所有牵涉到的内我的一个沟通网。那么，显然的，一个具体的群体事件暗示了一种在比例上会把你们科技性沟通比下去的内在沟通系统。", "en": "If you want to change your job, and hold that desire, a new job will come into your experience in precisely the same fashion, in that the inner events will be arranged by the inner ego. A body event involves the working of numerous muscles and joints and so forth. An event involving a job change concerns motion on the part of many people, and implies a network of communication on the part of all of the inner egos involved. Obviously, then, a mass physical event implies an inner system of communications of proportions that would put your technological communications to shame.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0982", "zh": "敌人是显而易见的，他的意图是邪恶的。战争基本是集体自杀的例子——不过，从事这种自杀的人，带着所有战争的行头，透过集体暗示，而且透过国家的伟大资源来实现它，这些人确信宇宙是不安全的、自己是不可信赖的，而陌生人是永远有敌意的。你理所当然的以为，人类是具侵略性而好战的。你必须在你自己被毁之前先下手为强。这些偏执性的倾向大半隐藏在国家主义之旗帜下。", "en": "The enemy is obvious. His intentions are evil. Wars are basically examples of mass suicide — embarked upon, however, with all of the battle’s paraphernalia, carried out through mass suggestion, and through the nation’s greatest resources, by men who are convinced that the universe is unsafe, that the self cannot be trusted, and that strangers are always hostile. You take it for granted that the species is aggressively combative. You must out-think the enemy nation before you yourself are destroyed. These paranoiac tendencies are largely hidden beneath man’s nationalistic banners.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第835节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "835", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e0995", "zh": "就时间而言，有天将会有一本厚书。虽然这稿子尚未以一本具体书的样子存在，但那书本身、那概念及字句，以最紧要的方式说来，在现在就是十分真实的。在所有各种的创作里暗示了某种特质，但却普遍被忽视了，因此，它们是不明显的。我们所涉及的这种创造性过程，能将某些那种特质显现出来，并且阐明人类心灵通常一直隐而不显的许多面貌。", "en": "Someday, in terms of time, there will be a thick book. Although the manuscript does not yet exist in a physical book, the book itself, the ideas and words, are in the most important fashions quite real now. Certain qualities are implied in all kinds of creativity that are generally overlooked, and so they are not apparent. The kind of creative procedures we are involved in can serve to bring some of those qualities to light, and to shed illumination upon many aspects of the human psyche that usually remain hidden.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第881节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "881", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-063-e1045", "zh": "也就是为了那个理由，它们才看起来彷佛掉出了「正常」领域之外。不过，这种特性却是自然人的基本属性。在科学方法的赞助下，它们显得不大对，因为科学方法本身就是被设定好来感知只适合它预见的模式的信息。这种能力显得是不可预知的、不连续的，只因为相对地，你们对事实上相当恒常不变的心理行为如此的不觉查。那是说，这种能力如此平顺、如此连续地运作，并且以如此轻易的方式（热切地），以至于只在某些情况下，你才对它们变得觉察。你们觉察到的好像是怪异特性的孤立暗示。", "en": "It is also for that reason that they seem to fall outside of the realm of the s-a-n-e (spelled). Such characteristics are, however, basic properties of the natural person. They do not appear very well under the auspices of the scientific method, because the scientific method is itself programmed to perceive only information that fits into its preconceived patterns. Such abilities appear to be unpredictable, discontinuous, only because you are so relatively unaware of what is actually quite constant psychological behavior. That is, such abilities operate so smoothly, so continuously, and with such ease (intently) that you become aware of them only under certain conditions. You are aware of what seem to be isolated hints of odd characteristics.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第4节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "4", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1052", "zh": "并没有像「杀戮本能」——如人们赋予这词汇的暗示和意义——这样的东西（热切地）。举例来说，在几乎无法对成人的你们描写的层面上，所有的婴儿都知道，他们是在一个只适合他们，而非任何一个别人的环境中——那是为他们的需要而剪裁的——的一个适当的位置里出生的。你们往往能以肤浅的方式看出，动物如何在「自然的条件」下，如此完美的适合它们的环境，因此它们的需要、欲望、设备与环境的特性如此的相合与结合。你们却并没能那么容易地看出，那同样适用于人、他的精神与物质环境、他的市镇或国家或文化，但是婴儿从出生的一刹那开始，就已会信赖。", "en": "There is no such thing as a killer instinct, with the implications and meaning that man gives that term (intently). At levels almost impossible to describe to you in your adulthoods, all infants, for example, know that they are born into the environmental niches that suit them and no others — [that are] tailored to their requirements. You can usually see in a superficial fashion how animals under “natural conditions” fit into their environments so perfectly, so that their needs and desires and equipment meet and merge with the characteristics of the environment. It is not nearly as easy to see that the same applies to man and his mental and physical environment, his town or country or culture, but the infant trusts from the very first moment.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第8节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "8", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-063-e1056", "zh": "这是一节非常短的课，不过，当你观察世界的事件，比如说，当今的世界局势（几天前开始的两伊战争）时，试着去扩大你知性所及的范围，因此你就能将世界事件认作是：对未来与过去的触机反应，而在现在形成的活生生的多重次元「小说」。以你们的说法，未来对过去的冲击——或不如说，未来对现在的暗示——是极为重要的。而这种预知性的反应，就与你通常认为对过去事件的反应一样的重要、众多且真实。（热切地。）", "en": "This will be a very brief session. When you look at world events, however, the present world situation for example (the war between Iraq and Iran, which began a few days ago), try to enlarge the scope of your intellectual reach, so that you consider world events as living multidimensional “novels” being formed in the present in response to both future and past triggers. The impact of the future on the past, in your terms — or rather, the implications of the future on the present — are highly important, and such precognitive reactions are as vital, numerous, and real as you ordinarily think that the reactions to past events are (intently).", "source": "神奇之道 · 第13节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "13", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 6}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 5}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 4}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 4}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 3}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 2}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 2}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 2}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 1}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 7, "quotes": 69, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 11, "only_en": 14}};
